# provoking-the-far-marker — plan 16 W3, the trigger as the player meets it.
#
# `DESIGN.md` § Wave-1 triggers: driving onto a spawn marker at least
# `wave_1_provocation_distance` (12) hexes from the core is what starts
# the list.  Nothing else in this file starts it — `schedule 3 4` only
# ARMS the mission's waves.
#
# ⚠ **Two markers, and the near one is the control.**  (11, 0) is a LIVE
# spawn source — it is outside the close-spawn-disable radius of 10, so
# wave 1 will use it once something wakes up — and it is inside the
# provocation distance, so standing on it does nothing at all.  A
# trigger with no distance test fires there, which is the marker a map
# author places to offer the player a safe look.
#
# ⚠ The player drives the whole way rather than being parked, because
# the trip is what the trigger COSTS: fourteen hexes out means being
# fourteen hexes from home at the moment the wave stands up.

echo provoking the far marker: eleven hexes is safe, fourteen is not

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 11 0
marker 11 0 spawn 3
click 14 0
marker 14 0 spawn 3
count markers 3 3

do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -1 -1 16 -1
drag -1 0 16 0
drag -1 1 16 1
count painted 54 54

# The mission's list, armed and waiting for its trigger.
schedule 3 4
waves 0 0

# Out to the NEAR marker, and stand on it.  It is a spawn source and it
# is not far enough to be worth poking.
park 0 0
drive 11 0
tick 10
vehicle 11 0
waves 0 0
count alive 0 0

# Three hexes further out is over the line.
drive 14 0
tick 4
vehicle 14 0
waves 1 1
count alive 3 3

# And the list does not re-arm under a player who stays parked on it:
# wave 2 waits for the clear and the lull, which never come here.
tick 30
waves 1 1

snap w3_provoking_the_far_marker
